; Full pre-labeled SMT-LIB corpus run (board #124). Test-only, outside the smt/
; firewall (I3). corpus_classify is the per-file classifier (one process per file,
; driven in parallel by corpus_run.sh under `timeout`); it links the same test-only
; parser + shipped Session the solver CLI uses. `make corpus-run`.

(executable
 (name corpus_classify)
 (modules corpus_classify)
 (libraries oxsmt_interface oxsmt_smtlib_parser oxsmt_euf))

; driver_equiv_test — the driver-equivalence guard (task #133). Shells out to BOTH the
; corpus_classify and oxsmt_cli executables over a deterministic file sample and asserts
; their verdicts agree, so the two drivers can never silently diverge again (a
; measurement-integrity hazard). Test-only, stdlib + Unix via harness_lib; it links NO
; smt/ library (it drives the built binaries, not the session).

(executable
 (name driver_equiv_test)
 (modules driver_equiv_test)
 (libraries harness_lib))
